The page calls stage 01 the same opening as Scattered Spider / MGM, and says stage 03's durable grant is what made Salesloft Drift and Vercel / Context.ai effective too.
notes:
Three related kill chains on csoh.org, and the page's related defense topics.

At stage 01 the page calls the phone call the same opening as Scattered Spider / MGM two years earlier, aimed at a different endpoint.

At stage 03 it says the same structural property, an OAuth grant that survives the call, made Salesloft Drift and Vercel / Context.ai so effective. Here it was reached by talking a person into creating the grant, rather than by stealing one that already existed.

The four defense topics the page links are SaaS security, IAM and cloud identity, data security, and incident response. SaaS is software as a service, SSPM is SaaS security posture management, and IAM is identity and access management.
